#58: 
This patch removes casting the values returned by memory allocation functions.

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*mgmt_tx)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct tx_complete_mon_data)...)
#74: FILE: drivers/staging/wilc1000/linux_mon.c:250:
+	mgmt_tx = kmalloc(sizeof(struct tx_complete_mon_data), GFP_ATOMIC);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

